{
  "method": "PCHIP or piecewise-linear interpolation of window chemical potentials vs observed mean Al fraction. Solve Maxwell equal-area along all increasing branches, require an interior pair supported globally over the measured interval, and retain the widest gap. Thinned grids keep both endpoint windows and alternate interior centers; the same subset is applied in quantum and classical samples. The differential is computed within each paired sample, not against a separately sampled historical bound.",
  "uncertainty": "Sensitivity values compare reconstructions on fixed window means. They quantify changes when varying the chosen windows and interpolation, not statistical confidence limits.",
